  "tagline": "Silver-lavender, starlit, quietly formal",
  "lineage": "New — not yet defined anywhere but here.",
  "story": "DRAFT — a sketch to rewrite in your own words. The guess, from the name: a colder, more elegant cousin of the night styles. Moonlight on frost, lavender shading into silver, a place that is formal without being stiff — an observatory ballroom. Where Starful Gothic is a pencil outdoors, Stelaine is engraved.",
  "mood": [
    "lunar",
    "elegant",
    "cool",
    "still"
  ],
  "principles": [
    "Lavender is a temperature, not a theme — it lives in the greys.",
    "Elegance by restraint: one hairline, one serif, lots of air.",
    "Light is reflected, never emitted: pale surfaces, silvered edges, no neon.",
    "Stillness — the layout holds a pose."
  ],
  "do": [
    "Set headings in a high-contrast serif with real tracking.",
    "Use hairline rules to structure the page.",
    "Keep the accent dusk-violet and rare."
  ],
  "dont": [
    "No saturated colour above a whisper.",
    "No heavy borders or loud shadows.",
    "No crowding; emptiness is part of the style."
  ],
  "voice": {
    "tone": "Composed and slightly formal, warm underneath.",
